Where each file sits in its tarball: marked lib/marked.umd.js, dompurify dist/purify.min.js, cdn-assets highlight.min.js
and styles/github{,-dark}.min.css (the highlight.js package itself has no browser build), github-markdown-css
github-markdown.css, mermaid dist/mermaid.min.js. Each library's license file is next to it as LICENSE-<name>
(dompurify also has LICENSE-MPL-dompurify).

Update: in a new empty temp folder run `npm pack <pkg>@<version> --ignore-scripts`, compare
`openssl dgst -sha512 -binary <tgz> | base64` with `npm view <pkg>@<version> dist.integrity`, check
`npm view <pkg>@<version> dist.attestations`, extract the files above and the license, replace them here and change
the table. Then run tests/md_open_test.sh (it renders a sample page in Chrome when one is installed).
